      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12152927::web::013::results_and_discussion",
        "PMC9098454::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed starting material is a single-phase, as-cast high-entropy alloy with minimal short-range order.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed starting material exhibits conventional electron–phonon-coupling-based superconductivity.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9329343::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Controlled annealing at different temperatures and durations followed by quenching can systematically vary short-range order.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Short-range order can be assessed using synchrotron X-ray or neutron total scattering.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tc can be determined using low-temperature electrical transport or magnetic susceptibility.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Measuring all samples from 2 to 10 K under identical cryogenic and magnetic-field conditions isolates Tc changes attributable to short-range order.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant structural mediator is local chemical clustering and short-range ordering within the lattice.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12152927::web::013::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Short-range ordering optimizes the local bonding environment.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An optimized local bonding environment improves electron–phonon coupling.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Improved electron–phonon coupling increases the superconducting energy gap.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Annealed specimens with greater short-range order will have systematically higher Tc than the as-cast baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12152927::web::013::results_and_discussion",
        "PMC9098454::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The shift in Tc will correlate positively with the degree of local ordering measured by total scattering.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12152927::web::013::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The effect should be most discernible in multi-principal-element alloys dominated by electron–phonon coupling.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Magnetic order, strong electronic correlations, or pronounced spin–orbit coupling may weaken or invert the relationship between short-range order and superconductivity.",
